                      === AETHERMUD NEWS ===

A Palladium Rifts roleplaying game. 62 races, 66 OCCs, 158 skills,
114 spells, 50 psionic powers, 449 playable rooms.

WHERE YOU CAN GO
  Americas   Chi-Town (Coalition capital and Burbs), Praxis (hub town),
             Tolkeen (mage city under siege), Horton and its wilderness
             ring, Lone Star (Coalition genetics complex), Puerto Angel,
             Lazlo.
  Atlantis   Splynn Dimensional Market, Alvurron, the Preserves,
             catacombs.
  Europe     New Camelot, NGR Germany (Triax tech).

  Character creation starts you in Chi-Town, Splynn, or New Camelot
  depending on the zone you pick. Praxis is reached by rift; you do not
  start there.

TRAVEL
  rift <destination>    pay universal credits, enter before it closes.
                        Others in the room can follow you through.
                        Moxim NPCs in Chi-Town, Splynn, New Camelot,
                        Tolkeen, Lazlo, and Praxis.
  hovertrain            Chi-Town Burbs to Horton.

COMBAT
  kill <target>         start combat, melee or ranged. Whatever weapon
                        you have wielded is what you fight with, so a
                        wielded rifle is fired for you each round. There
                        is no separate firing command.
  reload / unload       manage e-clips and ammo. An empty weapon clicks
                        and does no damage until you reload.
  autoparry             free parry against incoming attacks, on by
                        default.
  autododge             spend 1 APM per attack to dodge instead.
  stance                offensive, defensive, or standard.
  flee / stop           disengage.
  combat                show your attacks per melee and bonuses.

  Damage is pooled, not per-limb. Incoming hits burn through protective
  spell fields first, then your worn armor, then your own MDC or SDC and
  hit points. MDC weapons are needed to hurt MDC creatures.

MAGIC AND PSIONICS
  cast <spell>          spends PPE. Ley Line Walkers, Mystics, Shifters.
  psi <power>           spends ISP. Mind Melters and psychic OCCs.

TALKING TO PEOPLE
  There are no global chat channels on this game, by design.
  say / whisper / ooc   everyone in your room, and nobody outside it.
  telepathy             reach a player anywhere, if you have been
                        introduced to them and they are not shielded.
                        Costs ISP.
  radio                 requires a carried radio tuned to a shared
                        frequency.
  introduce / greet     how other players learn your name.
  tell                  contacts online staff only, not other players.

YOUR GEAR
  Weapons and armor you have wielded or worn stay with you when you
  quit. Loose items you are only carrying are dropped where you stand,
  so equip what you want to keep before logging out.

HELP AND REPORTING
  help                  category list. Then help <category>, then
                        help <topic>. help index shows everything.
  bug <message>         report something broken.
  typo <message>        report bad text.
  idea <message>        suggest something.
  who                   see who is online.

STILL BEING BUILT
  Deeper Chi-Town, Splynn, and NGR interiors. Stormshire and the
  Federation of Magic. Player housing and storage. More vehicle
  interiors. Skill help topics are thin: 119 of 158 skills have no help
  file yet.

Stay alive out there.
